<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Release entitlements (Runner / container app).

  Several omissions vs. Flutter's default Release.entitlements, each
  forced by Apple's AMFI rules + our current provisioning setup:

  1. `com.apple.developer.system-extension.install` — the provisioning
     profile authorizes it, but the moment it's effective, AMFI treats
     this binary as a System Extension host and forbids the hardened-
     runtime relaxations Flutter would otherwise need.
     (AMFI checks the *profile*-authorized entitlements, not the
     binary's claim, so simply omitting the key here is not enough on
     its own — see point #3.)

  2. `com.apple.security.application-groups` — absent because the
     provisioning profile does not currently grant App Groups. Policy
     and server config flow to the extension via
     `NETunnelProviderProtocol.providerConfiguration` instead.
     See `macos/Runner/DebugProfile.entitlements` for the steps to
     restore App Groups.

  3. Hardened-runtime relaxations (`allow-jit`,
     `allow-unsigned-executable-memory`, `disable-library-validation`)
     are also ABSENT here. Apple's AMFI rejects them as soon as the
     profile carries `system-extension.install`, regardless of whether
     the binary claims them, because the same kernel rule applies to
     anything that *could* host a System Extension under the active
     profile. Dropping them is fine for the release / AOT build —
     AOT-compiled Dart doesn't need JIT. Plugins that need
     `disable-library-validation` must be signed with the same team or
     dropped from the macOS embedder.

  TL;DR — until the dev portal's App ID `art.arcane.ArcaneDispatch` is
  reconfigured (drop SystemExtensions capability, optionally add App
  Groups), only the Release configuration can launch on a signed build.
  See README troubleshooting for the dev-portal walkthrough.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension</key>
	<array>
		<string>packet-tunnel-provider</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<false/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.server</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
